.TH "HED-CTAGS" "1" "2026-08-20" "hed v1.21.1" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-ctags \- Goto\-definition via a universal\-ctags tags file.
Owns both the :tag command and the underlying tag lookup (previously
src/utils/ctags.c).
.PP
Goto\-definition via a \c
.UR https://ctags.io/
universal\-ctags
.UE \c
\ \f[CR]tags\f[R] file.
Owns both the \f[CR]:tag\f[R] command and the underlying tag lookup
(previously \f[CR]src/utils/ctags.c\f[R]).
.SH Commands
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
T{
Command
T}@T{
Action
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]:tag <name>\f[R]
T}@T{
Jump to the definition of \f[CR]<name>\f[R]
T}
T{
\f[CR]:tag\f[R]
T}@T{
Jump to the definition of the word under the cursor
T}
.TE
.PP
After the jump the screen is centered on the target line.
.SH Keybind
Bound to \f[CR]gd\f[R] by default in \f[CR]src/config.c\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
cmapn(\[dq]gd\[dq], \[dq]tag\[dq], \[dq]goto tag\[dq]);
.EE
.SH How it works
The plugin shells out to \f[CR]rg\f[R] against a \f[CR]tags\f[R] file in
the current working directory (or any ancestor).
The expected format is the standard
\f[CR]TAG\[rs]tFILEPATH\[rs]tPATTERN\f[R] produced by:
.IP
.EX
ctags \-R .
.EE
.PP
No tags file → \f[CR]:tag\f[R] reports it and is a no\-op.
Regenerate whenever your project layout changes.
.SH Disable
Set \f[CR]plugin_load(&plugin_ctags, \&...)\f[R] to \f[CR]0\f[R] in
\f[CR]src/config.c\f[R] and \f[CR]:reload\f[R].
The \f[CR]gd\f[R] cmap will fall through to whatever else owns the
sequence (nothing, by default).
